From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dplayx: IDirectPlay4 stubs: GetPlayerFlags/Account/Address, GetGroupFlags/Owner, group connection settings, StartSession, SendChatMessage, CancelMessage, DestroyPlayer/Group messages, enumeration checks, SecureOpen

FIXME stubs of the DirectPlay 4 interface, as the conformance tests of dplayx
(and the documentation) have them. The service provider that DirectPlay
needs for every one of these is the one that was initialized; nothing here
asks for a network.

- GetPlayerFlags: DPERR_UNINITIALIZED without a provider, DPERR_INVALIDPARAMS
  for NULL, DPERR_INVALIDPLAYER for unknown ids, groups and the players the
  session keeps for itself (the system players, the host's name server and
  application server); DPPLAYER_LOCAL / SPECTATOR / SERVERPLAYER / OWNER.
- GetPlayerAccount: DPERR_NOSESSIONS, DPERR_UNSUPPORTED outside a secure
  session, DPERR_INVALIDFLAGS, DPERR_INVALIDPLAYER (nothing authenticates a
  player here, so none has an account; a missing buffer needs size 0).
- GetPlayerAddress (A and W): DPERR_UNSUPPORTED for DPID 0 and groups,
  DPERR_INVALIDPLAYER, and the provider's GetAddress for a player.
- GetGroupFlags, Get/SetGroupOwner, Get/SetGroupConnectionSettings and
  StartSession: the group must exist (DPERR_INVALIDGROUP); the owner,
  connection settings and starting a session are lobby session features:
  DPERR_UNSUPPORTED in any other session, the lobby provider's callback in
  a lobby session.
- SendChatMessage (A and W): validated, delivered to the local players as
  DPSYS_CHAT (the lobby provider's callback in a lobby session).
- CancelMessage / CancelPriority: the provider's Cancel with the message id
  (it was passed as a count before), DPERR_UNINITIALIZED, DPERR_UNSUPPORTED.
- SendEx remembers an asynchronous send that the provider keeps
  (DPERR_PENDING); IDirectPlaySP::SendComplete then gives the sender a
  DPSYS_SENDCOMPLETE message.
- DestroyPlayer / DestroyGroup: the provider is told the real flags, the
  other local players get DPSYS_DESTROYPLAYERORGROUP, the session's player
  count goes down, groups of a closed session are not walked.
- EnumPlayers / EnumGroups / EnumGroupPlayers / EnumGroupsInGroup:
  DPERR_NOSESSIONS without an open session (DPERR_GENERIC for a session that
  was only enumerated), DPERR_INVALIDPARAMS for NULL callbacks and
  DPENUMPLAYERS_SESSION without a guid; the system players of a peer and the
  host's hidden players are neither listed nor counted any more.
- CreateGroup: DPERR_INVALIDPARAMS without a session, and a peer that is not
  the host asks the host for the id like a player does (the id was made up
  locally before, which could collide).
- SecureOpen: parameter checks; credentials for a secure session are refused
  (DPERR_LOGONDENIED), nothing can check them.
- The name table reply (answer of older hosts) is ignored without FIXME.
- Class factory LockServer: the right answer, without FIXME.
- tests/dplayx.c: todo_wine removed where these now pass (uninitialized
  provider for GetPlayerAccount/Address/Flags and GetGroupOwner, CreateGroup,
  EnumPlayers and EnumGroups without a session).

